//@version=6
// =============================================================================
//  ORB + Heikin-Ashi Confirmation  —  intraday Opening Range Breakout strategy
// =============================================================================
//  Instrument-agnostic. Designed for 1-min or 5-min charts (any intraday TF that
//  divides the opening-range window; ≤ 15 min is enforced).
//
//  Four selectable entry variants (input "Entry variant") so each can be
//  backtested on identical data:
//    1. Classic ORB        raw close beyond OR high / low
//    2. HA confirmation    HA close beyond OR level, correct HA color, wrong-side
//                          wick ≤ X% of HA range, HA body ≥ Y% of HA range
//    3. HA + narrow range  variant 2, only on days where OR width ≤ k × prior-day ATR
//    4. Break & retest     raw close breaks the OR level; within N bars price
//                          retests the level and an HA candle closes back beyond it
//
//  Heikin-Ashi is computed INTERNALLY from the chart's real OHLC. Run this on a
//  normal candle chart: orders and fills use real prices; HA is only a filter.
//  (Running a strategy on an HA chart type would fill at synthetic HA prices.)
//
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  EXECUTION MODEL & SAME-BAR AMBIGUITY ASSUMPTIONS  (read before trusting results)
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  A. Signals are evaluated only on CONFIRMED bars (barstate.isconfirmed). An entry
//     is a market order sent at the signal bar's close and filled at the NEXT
//     bar's open (process_orders_on_close = false). Labels therefore show
//     "Entry ≈ signal close"; the real fill is the next open (+ slippage).
//  B. SL / TP1 / TP2 are attached at the same moment as the entry, so they are
//     live from the fill bar onward — including the fill bar itself.
//  C. If SL and a TP are both inside one bar's range, TradingView's broker
//     emulator does NOT know which came first. It assumes: if the open is nearer
//     the high, path = open → high → low → close; otherwise open → low → high →
//     close. This can flatter or hurt results. Mitigation: enable "Bar magnifier"
//     (Premium) in Properties, or compare 1-min vs 5-min results — a big gap means
//     results depend on intrabar path assumptions.
//  D. Break-even is applied at the CLOSE of the bar on which TP1 filled. If TP1
//     fills and price reverses to the original SL within that same bar, the runner
//     is stopped at the ORIGINAL SL (a live broker-side BE could do better). This
//     is deliberately conservative.
//  E. The TP1-already-exceeded filter uses the signal bar's close (known at
//     decision time). If the next open gaps beyond TP1, the trade is still taken
//     and the TP1 limit fills at that open (better-than-limit fill).
//  F. Hard time exit: on the bar whose close time ≥ the exit time (e.g. the
//     10:59 bar on 1-min, 10:55 bar on 5-min, closing at 11:00:00), the position
//     is closed AT THAT BAR'S CLOSE (strategy.close_all(immediately = true)).
//     No new entry is accepted if its fill would occur at/after the exit time.
//  G. HA-trail exit (after TP1) is decided at bar close and fills next open.
//  H. Only one position at a time: a new signal is ignored while in a position
//     (no stop-and-reverse). Max N trades/day and 1 per direction.
//  I. R-multiples are NET (include commission + slippage) and use the actual
//     fill price vs the initial stop: R = net P&L / (|fill − initial SL| × qty ×
//     point value). A break-even runner therefore prints slightly below 0R.
//
//  NO-REPAINT NOTES
//   • All decisions gated by barstate.isconfirmed; no future bars referenced.
//   • Prior-day ATR: request.security(..., "D", ta.atr(n), lookahead_off). With
//     lookahead_off the daily value can still be DEVELOPING on realtime bars, so
//     the script LATCHES the value from the last bar of the previous day (the
//     bar before timeframe.change("D")), which is the completed prior-day ATR on
//     both historical and realtime bars. The value is then frozen for the day.
// =============================================================================
// Header notes:
//  • Costs — set for YOUR instrument/broker (Properties tab overrides these):
//    0.01 % per side ≈ liquid stock/ETF or crypto taker fee; for futures switch to
//    strategy.commission.cash_per_contract (e.g. 2.25 per side). Slippage = ticks
//    added to every market/stop fill.
//  • margin_long/short = 0 disables emulated margin calls; size is controlled by
//    the sizing inputs (and optional leverage cap) instead.
//  • use_bar_magnifier: set true on a Premium plan for intrabar fill accuracy.
strategy(
  title                   = "ORB + Heikin-Ashi Confirmation",
  shorttitle              = "ORB-HA",
  overlay                 = true,
  initial_capital         = 100000,
  default_qty_type        = strategy.fixed,
  default_qty_value       = 1,
  pyramiding              = 0,
  commission_type         = strategy.commission.percent,
  commission_value        = 0.01,
  slippage                = 2,
  margin_long             = 0,
  margin_short            = 0,
  process_orders_on_close = false,
  calc_on_every_tick      = false,
  calc_on_order_fills     = false,
  use_bar_magnifier       = false,
  max_labels_count        = 500,
  max_bars_back           = 500)

// =============================================================================
//  INPUTS
// =============================================================================
const string GRP_SES  = "Session"
const string GRP_ENT  = "Entry"
const string GRP_RISK = "Risk & exits"
const string GRP_SIZE = "Position sizing"
const string GRP_VIS  = "Display"

const string V1 = "1 - Classic ORB (raw close)"
const string V2 = "2 - HA confirmation"
const string V3 = "3 - HA + narrow-range filter"
const string V4 = "4 - Break & retest (HA)"

const string SM_HA  = "HA candle extreme"
const string SM_MID = "OR midline"
const string SM_OPP = "Opposite OR side"

const string SZ_RISK  = "Risk % of equity"
const string SZ_FIXED = "Fixed quantity"

string tzIn         = input.string("America/New_York", "Session timezone (IANA)", group = GRP_SES)
string orSessIn     = input.session("0930-0945", "Opening range window", group = GRP_SES,
  tooltip = "Bars whose OPEN time falls in this window form the opening range.")
int    endHourIn    = input.int(11, "Hard exit / no-entry time  hh", minval = 0, maxval = 23, inline = "end", group = GRP_SES)
int    endMinIn     = input.int(0, "mm", minval = 0, maxval = 59, inline = "end", group = GRP_SES)

string variantIn    = input.string(V2, "Entry variant", options = [V1, V2, V3, V4], group = GRP_ENT)
float  wickMaxIn    = input.float(10.0, "HA wrong-side wick max (% of HA range)", minval = 0, maxval = 100, step = 1, group = GRP_ENT)
float  bodyMinIn    = input.float(30.0, "HA body min (% of HA range, doji filter)", minval = 0, maxval = 100, step = 1, group = GRP_ENT)
float  nrMultIn     = input.float(1.0, "Narrow range: OR width ≤ k × prior-day ATR", minval = 0.05, step = 0.05, group = GRP_ENT)
int    atrLenIn     = input.int(14, "Prior-day ATR length", minval = 1, group = GRP_ENT)
int    retestBarsIn = input.int(12, "Retest: expire after N bars", minval = 1, group = GRP_ENT)
int    retestTolIn  = input.int(0, "Retest: touch tolerance (ticks)", minval = 0, group = GRP_ENT,
  tooltip = "A retest counts if price comes within this many ticks of the OR level.")
bool   retestWickIn = input.bool(false, "Retest: also require no wrong-side wick", group = GRP_ENT,
  tooltip = "A genuine retest candle usually HAS a wick into the level, so this is off by default. Color + body filters always apply.")

string stopModeIn   = input.string(SM_HA, "Stop mode", options = [SM_HA, SM_MID, SM_OPP], group = GRP_RISK)
int    stopBufIn    = input.int(0, "Stop buffer (ticks)", minval = 0, group = GRP_RISK)
float  tp1MultIn    = input.float(1.0, "TP1 = OR level ± k × OR range", minval = 0.1, step = 0.1, group = GRP_RISK)
float  tp2MultIn    = input.float(2.0, "TP2 = OR level ± k × OR range", minval = 0.1, step = 0.1, group = GRP_RISK)
float  tp1PctIn     = input.float(50.0, "% of position closed at TP1", minval = 1, maxval = 99, group = GRP_RISK)
bool   moveBEIn     = input.bool(true, "Move runner stop to break-even after TP1", group = GRP_RISK)
int    beOffIn      = input.int(0, "Break-even offset (ticks, + = locks profit)", group = GRP_RISK)
bool   haTrailIn    = input.bool(false, "HA-trail exit after TP1", group = GRP_RISK,
  tooltip = "After TP1, close the runner when an opposite-color HA candle prints WITH a wrong-side wick (long: red HA candle with a lower wick > the wick threshold = bearish momentum).")
bool   skipTP1In    = input.bool(true, "Skip signal if close already beyond TP1", group = GRP_RISK)
int    maxTradesIn  = input.int(2, "Max trades per day", minval = 1, maxval = 2, group = GRP_RISK)

string sizeModeIn   = input.string(SZ_RISK, "Sizing mode", options = [SZ_RISK, SZ_FIXED], group = GRP_SIZE)
float  riskPctIn    = input.float(0.5, "Risk per trade (% of equity)", minval = 0.01, step = 0.05, group = GRP_SIZE)
float  fixedQtyIn   = input.float(2, "Fixed quantity", minval = 0, group = GRP_SIZE)
float  qtyStepIn    = input.float(1, "Quantity step (1 = shares/contracts)", minval = 0.00000001, group = GRP_SIZE,
  tooltip = "Order sizes are rounded down to a multiple of this. Each trade needs ≥ 2 steps so it can be split into TP1 + runner; smaller signals are skipped.")
float  maxLevIn     = input.float(0, "Max notional leverage (0 = off, risk mode only)", minval = 0, step = 0.5, group = GRP_SIZE)

bool   showLblIn    = input.bool(true, "Signal / exit labels", group = GRP_VIS)
bool   showTblIn    = input.bool(true, "Stats table (R-based)", group = GRP_VIS)

// =============================================================================
//  GUARDS
// =============================================================================
if barstate.isfirst
    if not timeframe.isintraday or timeframe.in_seconds() > 900
        runtime.error("ORB-HA: use an intraday chart of 15 minutes or less (1-min or 5-min recommended).")
    if tp2MultIn <= tp1MultIn
        runtime.error("ORB-HA: TP2 multiple must be greater than TP1 multiple.")

// =============================================================================
//  HEIKIN-ASHI (computed internally from real OHLC)
// =============================================================================
//  haClose = (O + H + L + C) / 4
//  haOpen  = (prev haOpen + prev haClose) / 2   (seeded with (O + C) / 2)
//  haHigh  = max(H, haOpen, haClose) ; haLow = min(L, haOpen, haClose)
float haClose = (open + high + low + close) / 4.0
float haOpen  = na
haOpen := na(haOpen[1]) ? (open + close) / 2.0 : (haOpen[1] + haClose[1]) / 2.0
float haHigh  = math.max(high, haOpen, haClose)
float haLow   = math.min(low, haOpen, haClose)

float haRange     = haHigh - haLow
float haBody      = math.abs(haClose - haOpen)
float haUpperWick = haHigh - math.max(haOpen, haClose)
float haLowerWick = math.min(haOpen, haClose) - haLow
bool  haGreen     = haClose > haOpen
bool  haRed       = haClose < haOpen

float wickMaxFrac = wickMaxIn / 100.0
float bodyMinFrac = bodyMinIn / 100.0

// Quality checks. "Wrong side" = the side against the trade:
//   long  → lower wick must be small (buyers in control the whole bar)
//   short → upper wick must be small
f_haLongOK(bool checkWick) =>
    bool ok = haGreen and haRange > 0 and haBody >= bodyMinFrac * haRange
    ok and (not checkWick or haLowerWick <= wickMaxFrac * haRange)

f_haShortOK(bool checkWick) =>
    bool ok = haRed and haRange > 0 and haBody >= bodyMinFrac * haRange
    ok and (not checkWick or haUpperWick <= wickMaxFrac * haRange)

// =============================================================================
//  SESSION / OPENING RANGE
// =============================================================================
bool inOR    = not na(time(timeframe.period, orSessIn, tzIn))
bool orStart = inOR and not inOR[1]
bool orDone  = not inOR and inOR[1]                 // first bar after the OR window

// Exit time for the CURRENT bar's calendar date in the session timezone.
int  endTs   = timestamp(tzIn, year(time, tzIn), month(time, tzIn), dayofmonth(time, tzIn), endHourIn, endMinIn)
bool pastEnd = time_close >= endTs                  // this bar closes at/after the exit time

var float orHigh      = na
var float orLow       = na
var bool  orReady     = false
var int   tradesToday = 0
var bool  longUsed    = false
var bool  shortUsed   = false

// Break & retest state (per direction)
var int  brkUpBar = na
var bool rtUpSeen = false
var int  brkDnBar = na
var bool rtDnSeen = false

if orStart                                          // new day: reset everything
    orHigh      := high
    orLow       := low
    orReady     := false
    tradesToday := 0
    longUsed    := false
    shortUsed   := false
    brkUpBar    := na
    rtUpSeen    := false
    brkDnBar    := na
    rtDnSeen    := false
else if inOR
    orHigh := math.max(orHigh, high)
    orLow  := math.min(orLow, low)

if orDone
    orReady := true
if pastEnd                                          // window over; also prevents a stale
    orReady := false                                // OR from trading pre-market next day

float orRange = orHigh - orLow
float orMid   = (orHigh + orLow) / 2.0

// Entry window: OR complete, and the next-bar fill would be before the exit time.
bool inWindow = orReady and not inOR and time_close < endTs

// =============================================================================
//  PRIOR-DAY ATR (non-repainting latch, lookahead_off)
// =============================================================================
float dailyAtr = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, "D", ta.atr(atrLenIn), lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_off)
var float priorDayAtr = na
if timeframe.change("D")
    // Value on the last bar of the previous daily session = completed prior-day ATR.
    priorDayAtr := dailyAtr[1]

bool  nrOK    = not na(priorDayAtr) and orRange > 0 and orRange <= nrMultIn * priorDayAtr
float nrRatio = priorDayAtr > 0 ? orRange / priorDayAtr : na

// =============================================================================
//  LEVELS
// =============================================================================
// TP anchors on the OR level (not the fill), so "price already beyond TP1 at the
// signal close" is a meaningful filter.
float tp1Long  = orHigh + tp1MultIn * orRange
float tp2Long  = orHigh + tp2MultIn * orRange
float tp1Short = orLow  - tp1MultIn * orRange
float tp2Short = orLow  - tp2MultIn * orRange

f_stop(bool isLong) =>
    float buf = stopBufIn * syminfo.mintick
    switch stopModeIn
        SM_HA  => isLong ? haLow - buf : haHigh + buf      // signal HA candle extreme
        SM_MID => isLong ? orMid - buf : orMid + buf
        => isLong ? orLow - buf : orHigh + buf             // opposite side of the OR

f_qty(float riskPerUnit) =>
    float q = sizeModeIn == SZ_FIXED ? fixedQtyIn :
      (strategy.equity * riskPctIn / 100.0) / (riskPerUnit * syminfo.pointvalue)
    if sizeModeIn == SZ_RISK and maxLevIn > 0
        q := math.min(q, strategy.equity * maxLevIn / (close * syminfo.pointvalue))
    math.floor(q / qtyStepIn) * qtyStepIn

// =============================================================================
//  BREAK & RETEST STATE MACHINE (variant 4)
// =============================================================================
float tol = retestTolIn * syminfo.mintick
if orReady
    // Expire / invalidate an armed setup
    if not na(brkUpBar) and (bar_index - brkUpBar > retestBarsIn or close < orLow or longUsed)
        brkUpBar := na
        rtUpSeen := false
    if not na(brkDnBar) and (bar_index - brkDnBar > retestBarsIn or close > orHigh or shortUsed)
        brkDnBar := na
        rtDnSeen := false
    // Record a retest touch (bars AFTER the break bar only)
    if not na(brkUpBar) and bar_index > brkUpBar and low <= orHigh + tol
        rtUpSeen := true
    if not na(brkDnBar) and bar_index > brkDnBar and high >= orLow - tol
        rtDnSeen := true

// Confirmation: retest already seen (may be this bar) and an HA candle of the
// right color + body closes back beyond the level.
bool retestLong  = not na(brkUpBar) and rtUpSeen and bar_index > brkUpBar and haClose > orHigh and f_haLongOK(retestWickIn)
bool retestShort = not na(brkDnBar) and rtDnSeen and bar_index > brkDnBar and haClose < orLow and f_haShortOK(retestWickIn)

// Arm a new break (first raw close across the level). Done after the signal
// check so the break bar itself can never be its own retest.
if orReady and inWindow
    if na(brkUpBar) and not longUsed and close > orHigh and close[1] <= orHigh
        brkUpBar := bar_index
        rtUpSeen := false
    if na(brkDnBar) and not shortUsed and close < orLow and close[1] >= orLow
        brkDnBar := bar_index
        rtDnSeen := false

// =============================================================================
//  RAW SIGNALS PER VARIANT
// =============================================================================
bool haLongSig  = haClose > orHigh and f_haLongOK(true)
bool haShortSig = haClose < orLow  and f_haShortOK(true)

bool rawLong = switch variantIn
    V1 => close > orHigh
    V2 => haLongSig
    V3 => haLongSig and nrOK
    => retestLong

bool rawShort = switch variantIn
    V1 => close < orLow
    V2 => haShortSig
    V3 => haShortSig and nrOK
    => retestShort

bool canTrade = barstate.isconfirmed and inWindow and orRange > 0 and
  strategy.position_size == 0 and tradesToday < maxTradesIn

bool candLong  = canTrade and not longUsed  and rawLong
bool candShort = canTrade and not shortUsed and rawShort

// Skip signals where the move is already done (close beyond TP1).
bool skipLong  = candLong  and skipTP1In and close >= tp1Long
bool skipShort = candShort and skipTP1In and close <= tp1Short

bool goLong  = candLong  and not skipLong
bool goShort = candShort and not skipShort and not goLong

// =============================================================================
//  TRADE STATE
// =============================================================================
var bool   trActive   = false
var int    trDir      = 0
var int    trSigBar   = na
var float  trSLInit   = na
var float  curStop    = na
var float  curTP1     = na
var float  curTP2     = na
var bool   tp1Done    = false
var bool   beMoved    = false
var float  trPnl      = 0.0
var float  trRiskCash = 0.0
var int    seenClosed = 0

// Stats (R-based, per complete trade = both legs blended)
var array<float> tradeR = array.new<float>()
var int skippedTP1 = 0
var int skippedSize = 0

f_px(float p) => str.tostring(p, format.mintick)
f_r(float r)  => (r >= 0 ? "+" : "") + str.tostring(r, "0.00") + "R"

// Housekeeping: when flat, make sure no stale exit orders survive to the next
// trade with the same entry id.
if barstate.isconfirmed and strategy.position_size == 0
    strategy.cancel("L-TP1")
    strategy.cancel("L-TP2")
    strategy.cancel("S-TP1")
    strategy.cancel("S-TP2")

// ── Process newly closed legs: labels, R-multiples, exit alerts ─────────────
if barstate.isconfirmed and strategy.closedtrades > seenClosed
    for i = seenClosed to strategy.closedtrades - 1
        float  ep   = strategy.closedtrades.entry_price(i)
        float  xp   = strategy.closedtrades.exit_price(i)
        float  sz   = math.abs(strategy.closedtrades.size(i))
        float  pnl  = strategy.closedtrades.profit(i)
        float  rc   = math.abs(ep - trSLInit) * sz * syminfo.pointvalue
        float  legR = rc > 0 ? pnl / rc : na
        string why  = strategy.closedtrades.exit_comment(i)
        bool   isL  = strategy.closedtrades.size(i) > 0
        trPnl      += pnl
        trRiskCash += rc
        if why == "TP1"
            tp1Done := true
        if showLblIn
            label.new(bar_index, isL ? high : low, why + " " + f_r(legR) + "\n@ " + f_px(xp),
              yloc = isL ? yloc.abovebar : yloc.belowbar,
              style = isL ? label.style_label_down : label.style_label_up,
              color = legR >= 0 ? color.new(color.green, 15) : color.new(color.red, 15),
              textcolor = color.white, size = size.small)
        alert(str.format("ORB-HA EXIT {0} {1} | reason: {2} | qty {3} @ {4} | leg {5}",
              syminfo.ticker, isL ? "LONG" : "SHORT", why, str.tostring(sz), f_px(xp), f_r(legR)),
              alert.freq_once_per_bar_close)
    seenClosed := strategy.closedtrades

// ── Trade complete → blended R, stats, alert ─────────────────────────────────
if barstate.isconfirmed and trActive and strategy.position_size == 0 and trRiskCash > 0
    float totR = trPnl / trRiskCash
    array.push(tradeR, totR)
    if showLblIn
        label.new(bar_index, trDir > 0 ? high : low, "TRADE " + f_r(totR),
          yloc = trDir > 0 ? yloc.abovebar : yloc.belowbar,
          style = label.style_none, textcolor = totR >= 0 ? color.green : color.red, size = size.normal)
    alert(str.format("ORB-HA TRADE CLOSED {0} {1} | total {2} (net, blended legs)",
          syminfo.ticker, trDir > 0 ? "LONG" : "SHORT", f_r(totR)), alert.freq_once_per_bar_close)
    trActive := false
else if trActive and strategy.position_size == 0 and trRiskCash == 0 and bar_index > trSigBar + 1
    trActive := false                                    // entry never filled (safety)

// ── After TP1: runner stop → break-even ─────────────────────────────────────
if barstate.isconfirmed and moveBEIn and tp1Done and not beMoved and strategy.position_size != 0
    float off = beOffIn * syminfo.mintick
    if strategy.position_size > 0
        float be = strategy.position_avg_price + off
        strategy.exit("L-TP2", "L", limit = curTP2, stop = be, comment_profit = "TP2", comment_loss = "BE")
        curStop := be
    else
        float be = strategy.position_avg_price - off
        strategy.exit("S-TP2", "S", limit = curTP2, stop = be, comment_profit = "TP2", comment_loss = "BE")
        curStop := be
    beMoved := true
    alert(str.format("ORB-HA {0} TP1 filled - runner stop moved to break-even {1}", syminfo.ticker, f_px(curStop)),
          alert.freq_once_per_bar_close)

// ── Optional HA-trail exit after TP1 (assumption G) ──────────────────────────
// Long: opposite-color (red) HA candle WITH a lower ("wrong-side") wick → close.
// Short: green HA candle WITH an upper wick → close.
if barstate.isconfirmed and haTrailIn and tp1Done and not pastEnd and haRange > 0
    if strategy.position_size > 0 and haRed and haLowerWick > wickMaxFrac * haRange
        strategy.close("L", comment = "HA trail")
    else if strategy.position_size < 0 and haGreen and haUpperWick > wickMaxFrac * haRange
        strategy.close("S", comment = "HA trail")

// ── Hard time exit (assumption F) ────────────────────────────────────────────
// Placed after leg processing so a same-bar close is booked on the next bar
// consistently (closedtrades and position size never get out of step).
if barstate.isconfirmed and pastEnd and strategy.position_size != 0
    strategy.close_all(comment = "Time exit", immediately = true)

// =============================================================================
//  ENTRIES  (each order carries a full SL / TP1 / TP2 bracket)
// =============================================================================
if skipLong or skipShort
    skippedTP1 += 1

if goLong or goShort
    bool  isL  = goLong
    float sl   = f_stop(isL)
    float tp1  = isL ? tp1Long : tp1Short
    float tp2  = isL ? tp2Long : tp2Short
    float risk = isL ? close - sl : sl - close
    float q    = risk > 0 ? f_qty(risk) : 0.0
    float q1   = math.floor(q * tp1PctIn / 100.0 / qtyStepIn) * qtyStepIn
    bool  qtyOK = risk > 0 and q1 >= qtyStepIn and (q - q1) >= qtyStepIn * 0.999999
    if not qtyOK
        skippedSize += 1
    else
        string sig = isL ? "LONG" : "SHORT"
        string msg = str.format("ORB-HA ENTRY {0} {1} [{2}] | entry ~{3} (next open) | SL {4} | TP1 {5} ({6}%) | TP2 {7} | qty {8} | 1R = {9}",
              syminfo.ticker, sig, variantIn, f_px(close), f_px(sl), f_px(tp1), str.tostring(tp1PctIn),
              f_px(tp2), str.tostring(q), f_px(risk))
        if isL
            strategy.entry("L", strategy.long, qty = q, comment = "ORB L", alert_message = msg)
            strategy.exit("L-TP1", "L", qty = q1, limit = tp1, stop = sl, comment_profit = "TP1", comment_loss = "SL")
            strategy.exit("L-TP2", "L", limit = tp2, stop = sl, comment_profit = "TP2", comment_loss = "SL")
            longUsed := true
        else
            strategy.entry("S", strategy.short, qty = q, comment = "ORB S", alert_message = msg)
            strategy.exit("S-TP1", "S", qty = q1, limit = tp1, stop = sl, comment_profit = "TP1", comment_loss = "SL")
            strategy.exit("S-TP2", "S", limit = tp2, stop = sl, comment_profit = "TP2", comment_loss = "SL")
            shortUsed := true
        tradesToday += 1
        trActive   := true
        trDir      := isL ? 1 : -1
        trSigBar   := bar_index
        trSLInit   := sl
        curStop    := sl
        curTP1     := tp1
        curTP2     := tp2
        tp1Done    := false
        beMoved    := false
        trPnl      := 0.0
        trRiskCash := 0.0
        if showLblIn
            label.new(bar_index, isL ? low : high,
              sig + "  " + variantIn + "\nEntry ~" + f_px(close) + "\nSL  " + f_px(sl) +
              "\nTP1 " + f_px(tp1) + "\nTP2 " + f_px(tp2) + "\n1R = " + f_px(risk),
              yloc = isL ? yloc.belowbar : yloc.abovebar,
              style = isL ? label.style_label_up : label.style_label_down,
              color = isL ? color.new(color.teal, 0) : color.new(color.maroon, 0),
              textcolor = color.white, size = size.small)
        alert(msg, alert.freq_once_per_bar_close)

// =============================================================================
//  PLOTS
// =============================================================================
bool showOR = orReady or inOR
plot(showOR ? orHigh : na, "OR high", color.new(color.teal, 0), 2, plot.style_linebr)
plot(showOR ? orLow  : na, "OR low",  color.new(color.maroon, 0), 2, plot.style_linebr)
plot(showOR ? orMid  : na, "OR mid",  color.new(color.gray, 40), 1, plot.style_linebr)
bgcolor(inOR ? color.new(color.blue, 92) : na, title = "OR window")

bool inPos = strategy.position_size != 0
plot(inPos ? strategy.position_avg_price : na, "Entry", color.new(color.white, 0), 1, plot.style_linebr)
plot(inPos ? curStop : na, "Stop", color.new(color.red, 0), 2, plot.style_linebr)
plot(inPos and not tp1Done ? curTP1 : na, "TP1", color.new(color.lime, 0), 1, plot.style_linebr)
plot(inPos ? curTP2 : na, "TP2", color.new(color.green, 0), 2, plot.style_linebr)

plotshape(skipLong,  "Skipped long (beyond TP1)",  shape.xcross, location.abovebar, color.new(color.orange, 0), size = size.tiny)
plotshape(skipShort, "Skipped short (beyond TP1)", shape.xcross, location.belowbar, color.new(color.orange, 0), size = size.tiny)

// =============================================================================
//  STATS TABLE (R-based — TradingView's report does not show avg R)
// =============================================================================
var table stats = table.new(position.top_right, 2, 9, bgcolor = color.new(color.black, 20),
  border_color = color.new(color.gray, 60), border_width = 1)

if showTblIn and barstate.islast
    int   n      = array.size(tradeR)
    int   wins   = 0
    float grossW = 0.0
    float grossL = 0.0
    float cum    = 0.0
    float peak   = 0.0
    float maxDD  = 0.0
    if n > 0
        for r in tradeR
            if r > 0
                wins   += 1
                grossW += r
            else
                grossL += -r
            cum   += r
            peak  := math.max(peak, cum)
            maxDD := math.max(maxDD, peak - cum)
    float avgR = n > 0 ? cum / n : na
    float pf   = grossL > 0 ? grossW / grossL : na
    float wr   = n > 0 ? 100.0 * wins / n : na
    table.cell(stats, 0, 0, "Variant",        text_color = color.white, text_halign = text.align_left)
    table.cell(stats, 1, 0, variantIn,        text_color = color.white)
    table.cell(stats, 0, 1, "Trades",         text_color = color.white, text_halign = text.align_left)
    table.cell(stats, 1, 1, str.tostring(n),  text_color = color.white)
    table.cell(stats, 0, 2, "Win % (R>0)",    text_color = color.white, text_halign = text.align_left)
    table.cell(stats, 1, 2, str.tostring(wr, "0.0") + "%", text_color = color.white)
    table.cell(stats, 0, 3, "Avg R (net)",    text_color = color.white, text_halign = text.align_left)
    table.cell(stats, 1, 3, str.tostring(avgR, "0.000"), text_color = avgR >= 0 ? color.lime : color.red)
    table.cell(stats, 0, 4, "PF (R)",         text_color = color.white, text_halign = text.align_left)
    table.cell(stats, 1, 4, str.tostring(pf, "0.00"), text_color = color.white)
    table.cell(stats, 0, 5, "Max DD (R)",     text_color = color.white, text_halign = text.align_left)
    table.cell(stats, 1, 5, str.tostring(maxDD, "0.00"), text_color = color.white)
    table.cell(stats, 0, 6, "Total R",        text_color = color.white, text_halign = text.align_left)
    table.cell(stats, 1, 6, str.tostring(cum, "0.00"), text_color = cum >= 0 ? color.lime : color.red)
    table.cell(stats, 0, 7, "Skipped bars (TP1 / size)", text_color = color.white, text_halign = text.align_left)
    table.cell(stats, 1, 7, str.tostring(skippedTP1) + " / " + str.tostring(skippedSize), text_color = color.white)
    table.cell(stats, 0, 8, "Today OR / prior ATR", text_color = color.white, text_halign = text.align_left)
    table.cell(stats, 1, 8, str.tostring(nrRatio, "0.00"), text_color = color.white)
